# The build context is uploaded to the Docker daemon in full before any COPY
# runs, so anything the Dockerfile never copies is pure transfer and memory
# cost inside the VM. `data/` alone holds multi-gigabyte snapshots (the
# Netherlands PBF, the verkeersborden CSV, the reference gpkg files) and is
# bind-mounted at runtime rather than baked into the image — shipping it as
# build context is what exhausts a default-sized Docker Desktop VM.
data/
.venv/
.git/
.gitignore

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

.DS_Store
.env
